roup":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["BCO 38-1 case without process","retroactive application of amended BCO","complaint vs. appeal","confession of sin","judicially out of order","remand","50th General Assembly BCO amendment"],"standard_of_review":"not_reached","case_numbers":["2023-19"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"A filing challenging Presbytery’s handling of Huffman’s BCO 38-1 confession was styled as an appeal under a newly amended rule. The SJC found it judicially out of order because the case began and was nearly completed when the former rule provided review by complaint, and retroactive application would be unfair. It remanded for Presbytery to adjudicate the filing as a complaint at its next stated meeting; denial or failure to act permits review by the SJC. No merits issue was decided."}},{"id":"bco:35-8--case:cases/ga22_1994__1993-05.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga22_1994__1993-05.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Clark v. Southwest Presbytery (Request for Clarification)","year":1995,"disposition":"administrative","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga22_1994__1993-05.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga22_1994__1993-05.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:35-8--case:cases/ga22_1994__1993-05.md:occ-d509fa62ebd8","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga22_1994__1993-05.html","repository_path":"cases/ga22_1994__1993-05.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":147},"excerpt":"The second argument by the Respondent was that the BCO 35-8 created","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga22_1994__1993-05.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["jurisdiction","church property","congregational withdrawal","civil corporation","ecclesiastical entity"],"standard_of_review":"not_state